@startuml senku-thread-lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Senku Thread Ownership and Lifecycle

actor "Caller threads" as Callers
participant "SenkuIngestor\nno owned thread" as Ingestor
participant "Shared runtime state\nAtomicReference firstFailure\nCountDownLatch maintenanceFinished\ncontrol lock + admission Condition" as Runtime
participant "Maintenance coordinator\none non-daemon scheduled thread" as Coordinator
participant "Maintenance pool\nup to maintenanceThreads\nnon-daemon workers\nbounded FIFO queue" as Workers
participant "Shared flush pool\ntarget <= 4 daemon workers\n192 MiB page-byte reservations" as FlushWorkers
database "Committed flushes and runs" as Files

note over Ingestor, Files
There is no Senku-owned Directory call lock.
The configured Directory must permit concurrent calls
on independent paths. A concurrent publication may
appear in the current or next scan.
Returned readers and writers are thread-confined.
end note

== WRITING ==
Callers -> Ingestor : put(key, value) / putLongs(keys, offset, length)
loop while paused or rotation requested
  Ingestor -> Runtime : await admission Condition using control lock\nbatch waits are interruptible
  Runtime --> Ingestor : wake; release control lock
end
Ingestor -> Ingestor : hash/group outside mutation locks\nacquire one stripe; insert/merge and sample count\nbatch hold <= 64 keys; unlock
alt sampled count below limit
  Ingestor --> Callers : return
else rotation requested and no active flush
  Ingestor -> Runtime : acquire control lock
  Ingestor -> Ingestor : acquire all mutation locks\ndetach active maps; install new maps\nunlock all mutations
  Ingestor -> Runtime : clear rotation request; signal; unlock
  Ingestor -> FlushWorkers : sort shard ranges and oversized long-set subranges\nprepare bounded pages (built-in longs)
  FlushWorkers --> Ingestor : encoded/compressed pages in requested order
  Ingestor -> Files : append pages sequentially\ncommit parts and shard index\npublish flush manifest last
  note over Callers, Files
  Other callers write to the new active stripes
  while the detached immutable batch is flushed.
  Only one detached batch exists at a time.
  end note
  Ingestor -> Runtime : acquire control lock\nrelease detached batch; signal; unlock
  Ingestor --> Callers : return
end

loop once every three seconds
  Coordinator -> Files : discover logical directory hierarchy\ncheck manifests; parse only new publications
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : select bottom-up\nflush->L0, L0->L1, ...
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : reserve exact inputs
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : allocate output run ID
  Coordinator -> Workers : enqueue reserved jobs\nuntil bounded FIFO queue is full
  alt queue full and eligible work remains unqueued
    Coordinator -> Ingestor : setPaused(true) using control lock
  else queue has capacity and no eligible work remains unqueued
    Coordinator -> Ingestor : setPaused(false); signal admission
  end
  Workers -> Files : merge; close input readers\npublish output manifest last
  Workers --> Coordinator : immutable completed-run result
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : accept output; replace catalog
  Coordinator -> Files : delete replaced inputs
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : coalesce completion wake\nrefill from catalog; refresh pause\nno discovery I/O
end

note over Coordinator, Files
Exactly one L0 batch may be active.
Only the coordinator owns its state; it needs no lock.
L0 flush inputs remain reserved until every shard succeeds.
Each worker publishes its run. The coordinator then accepts
the complete L0 batch and deletes the shared flush inputs.
Queued jobs are never reprioritized.
end note

== finishWriting() ==
Callers -> Ingestor : close admission using control lock\nclear pause; signal all
Ingestor -> Runtime : await any detached flush\nusing control lock Condition
Ingestor -> Ingestor : acquire all mutation locks\ndetach non-empty remainder\nunlock mutations
Ingestor -> Files : traverse and publish final detached flush
Ingestor -> Coordinator : enter drain mode immediately
Ingestor -> Runtime : await maintenanceFinished\nwithout writing lock
Coordinator -> Files : strictly reconcile hierarchy immediately\nreread all committed manifests
loop until a fresh scan sees no flushes/jobs and one terminal run per shard
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : select eligible work\nfrom the refreshed catalog
  note right of Coordinator
  Partial run merges wait until no flushes
  and no active L0 batch remain.
  Full fan-in merges remain eligible.
  end note
  Coordinator -> Workers : submit bounded merge jobs
  Workers -> Files : merge; close input readers\npublish output manifest last
  Workers --> Coordinator : immutable completed-run result
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : accept output; replace catalog
  Coordinator -> Files : delete replaced inputs
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : coalesce immediate scheduling wake\nrefill from catalog without discovery
  alt catalog appears drained
    Coordinator -> Files : strict hierarchy reconciliation\nreread all manifests before readiness
  end
end
note over Coordinator, Workers
After completion, a worker takes the next already-queued job.
Completions queue a lightweight scheduling wake in both states.
Periodic ticks still discover new publications.
Readiness is never published from cached completion counts.
end note
Coordinator -> Workers : shut down worker executor
Coordinator -> Coordinator : shut down scheduled executor
Coordinator -> Runtime : countDown maintenanceFinished
Runtime --> Ingestor : wake
Ingestor -> Coordinator : await both executor terminations
Ingestor --> Callers : transfer same exclusive .lock\nreturn SenkuReady

note over Callers, Files
READY owns no background threads.
READY retains the exclusive root .lock.
openStream() runs on its caller thread.
Terminal shard levels may differ.
end note

== First failure during WRITING or finalization ==
alt maintenance worker reports failure
  Workers -> Runtime : compareAndSet(null, failure)
  Workers --> Coordinator : failure result; readers closed
else caller-thread flush reports failure
  Ingestor -> Runtime : compareAndSet(null, failure)
  Ingestor -> Coordinator : wake failure handling
  Ingestor --> Callers : release detached maps and control lock\nthrow immediately
end
Coordinator -> Runtime : read primary failure; enter ERROR
Coordinator -> Ingestor : fail; clear pause; signal admission
Coordinator -> Coordinator : stop scans and submissions\ndiscard unsubmitted jobs
Coordinator -> Workers : clear queued jobs; shutdown\ndo not interrupt running jobs
Workers -> Files : close owned resources\nperform no explicit file deletion
Workers --> Coordinator : running jobs return
Coordinator -> Coordinator : wait for worker termination\nno catalog or filesystem cleanup
Coordinator -> Ingestor : await caller-owned detached flush\nrelease control lock while waiting
Coordinator -> Runtime : release exclusive root .lock
Coordinator -> Coordinator : shut down scheduled executor
Coordinator -> Runtime : countDown maintenanceFinished
Runtime --> Ingestor : if finishWriting is waiting, wake
Ingestor -> Coordinator : if finishWriting is active,\nawait both executor terminations
Ingestor --> Callers : if finishWriting was active,\nreport original first failure

note over Callers, Workers
An active put() or flush does not poll firstFailure.
Later ingestion calls receive only a generic ERROR-state failure.
An active finishWriting() awaits maintenanceFinished.
It preserves the recorded first failure and worker cause.
If that waiting caller is interrupted, finish shutdown and restore its flag.
Only the coordinator counts down maintenanceFinished.
A SenkuReady retains the root .lock until close releases it.
Writing shutdown releases its root .lock after workers and caller flush stop.
The invalid directory may contain partial artifacts
and must be deleted externally.
end note
@enduml
